# Generated media and per-project working dirs.
#
# ANCHORED WITH A LEADING SLASH, AND THAT IS NOT COSMETIC. A pattern like `projects/` —
# no leading slash, trailing slash — matches a directory of that name at EVERY depth, so
# it silently swallowed `apps/web/app/api/projects/**`: the library listing, the project
# GET/DELETE, /edit, /rerender and the route that flips `shared: true`. Five source files,
# the whole of the owner-scoped enforcement surface, untracked. `git status` says nothing
# about an ignored file, so the only symptom was that a fresh clone had no such routes —
# which nobody was going to notice until the first deploy served 404s at every one of them.
# Anchoring is the fix rather than a `!apps/web/...` re-inclusion pair, because the intent
# was always the three working dirs at the repo root and only those. Verify with
# `git check-ignore -v apps/web/app/api/projects/route.ts`, which must now print nothing.
/.inkcast/
/projects/
/renders/
*.mp4
# The approved public landing-page film ships with the site.
!/apps/web/public/showcase/gps-v4.mp4
*.wav
*.webm
!assets/**/*.wav

# Model weights fetched at runtime (Kokoro ONNX, etc.)
.models/

# Env
.env
.env.local
.env*.local
!.env.example

# Screenshot gate output — `scripts/screens.mjs` writes ~70 PNGs and a report per run.
# Untracked on purpose: they are evidence for one commit, not an artifact to carry.
/.screens/

.DS_Store
*.log
.pnpm-store/
playwright-report/
test-results/
